+# Upstream merge report — 5d290a609 (v0.347.0-nightly.0)
+
+## Merge identity
+
+- Range: `origin/denkhaus..upstream/main`, 6 commits, newest subject
+  `Merge pull request #844 from fabro-sh/remove/expired-secret-migrations`.
+- Fork tip before: `da12258b3` (seeds sync 2026-09-05); upstream tip: `5d290a609`.
+- Run branch aligned to `origin/denkhaus` first (fast-forward of the seeds sync),
+  then `git merge upstream/main --no-commit`.
+
+## Conflicts resolved by class
+
+- **1 conflict total** — `lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/pipeline/finalize.rs`,
+  import-block widening (known class, cf. 2026-08-31). Our side:
+  `use crate::context::keys;` (exit-kind plumbing, `keys::INTERNAL_EXIT_KIND`,
+  seeds fabro-08b4/67e5 line). Upstream side: `use crate::billing_rollup;`
+  (new module re-exporting the billing-rollup types that moved to
+  `lib/foundation/fabro-types/src/billing_rollup.rs`). Resolution: keep BOTH
+  imports (both used in the merged body — ours at the exit-kind reads,
+  upstream's at the two `billing_rollup_from_projection` call sites),
+  alphabetical order. No other conflict classes appeared.
+- No add/add test conflicts, no signature drift against our call sites, no
+  upstream-deleted files with fork deltas (verified: intersection of fork-delta
+  and upstream-deleted paths is empty).
+
+## Verification commands + results
+
+| Command | Result |
+|---|---|
+| `cargo build --workspace` | green |
+| `just qualitygate` | GATE GREEN — root manifest/lock changed (version bump), so the script ran fmt + `cargo check --workspace` per its own rule |
+| `cargo +nightly-2026-04-14 clippy -p fabro-cli -p fabro-server -p fabro-store -p fabro-workflow -p fabro-types --all-targets -- -D warnings` | clean (supplemental: the gate script degrades to check-only on root-manifest diffs; this restores the expected near-full gate for the merge-touched crates and doubles as the policy-mandated test compile) |
+| `cargo nextest run` on the same 5 crates (full 4457-test run, twice) | 4456/4457 pass in both runs |
+| `cargo nextest run -p fabro-workflow -E 'test(pipeline::finalize)'` | 26/26 (publish-blocked + boundary taxonomy touchpoints) |
+| `cargo nextest run -p fabro-workflow -E 'test(seed_cycles)'` | 4/4 (fabro-45d0 re-attachment intact) |
+| `cargo nextest run -p fabro-server -E 'test(publish_blocked)'` | 2/2 (Slack lifecycle remediation intact) |
+
+Flake notes (environmental, not merge regressions):
+- `fabro-workflow handler::parallel::tests::for_each_accepts_an_array_at_the_item_limit`
+  timed out under full-suite load — the DOCUMENTED fabro-80b3 class named in
+  `scripts/qualitygate.nu`; passes isolated (3.7s, marked slow).
+- `fabro-server server::tests::pull_request_creation_persists_generation_failure`
+  failed once under 5-crate load, then passed standalone, in the package-level
+  run, and in the repeat 5-crate run. The upstream diff provably does not touch
+  its helpers (`pr_test_app_with_completed_run`, supervisor, polling helper).
+
+## Obsolescence notes (seeds/features upstream now supersedes)
+
+- **None.** No fork seed is superseded by this range. Our fork had zero delta on
+  `lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/billing_rollup.rs`, `lib/apps/fabro-server/src/startup.rs`,
+  and `lib/apps/fabro-server/src/migrations.rs`, so upstream's reshapes there
+  were clean takes.
+- fabro-b7c4 (legacy run-catalog key acceptance): local fix `31809f2ad`
+  untouched by this range; upstream still lacks it, PR offer still valid.
+- Watchlist unchanged: no exit-kind/publish-blocked equivalent upstream; no
+  node-on-failure adoption for `develop`.
+
+## What it means for us — per upstream theme
+
+- **Version bump to 0.347.0-nightly.0**: routine.
+- **Rebuild conclusion stage summaries from run events (PR #842)**: replayed/
+  projected conclusions now rebuild from the event log in
+  `lib/components/fabro-store/src/run_state.rs` instead of trusting
+  finalize-time persistence; `finalize.rs` shrinks. For us: our terminal-event
+  taxonomy (publish-blocked, boundary, deadlock/soft-stop) classifies the SAME
+  events the rebuild reads — replay and live conclusion stay consistent with no
+  fork adaptation needed; keep building terminal-semantics work on the event
+  stream, not on extra persisted state.
+- **Billing rollup types moved to `fabro-types`** (re-exported from
+  `fabro-workflow`): a foundation-level home for rollup shapes. For us: any
+  fork usage should import from the re-export as `finalize.rs` now does; no
+  parallel type.
+- **Remove expired startup secret migrations (PR #844)**: deletes the two
+  expired 2026-05 migrations and their tests, shrinking `startup.rs` by ~246
+  lines. For us: smaller startup surface, docs
+  (`docs/internal/server-secrets-strategy.md`,
+  `docs/internal/migrations-strategy.md`) updated upstream — our secrets flow
+  rides upstream's; nothing fork-local to re-attach.
