 {"id":"fabro-e988","title":"Print critical-first failure summary in the qualitygate script","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T17:28:57.277Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T17:28:57.277Z","description":"Change scripts/qualitygate.nu (wired via the qualitygate recipe in justfile): on failure, print a compact summary first — failing step name plus the ^error lines grepped from the log — before the full output. Basis: in run 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN, tester@2's ~10 KB failure message buried the two decisive clippy errors at the very end; implementer@3 saw only a preview cut mid-log and had to open the blob to learn what broke. Expected effect: the re-entering implementer reads the actual error inline — faster, cheaper rework; composes with fabro-0d56. Basis: run 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN, workflow version af625ca581c5947f51dfa5597eb67892e0bee5d71ae041130412d1a54873ce8e, commit ecbd4d47c4c6d3272035e535731bc14f61a20662","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-c3b4","title":"Use a top-N sd ready view in the planner instead of the full firehose","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T17:28:57.532Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T17:28:57.532Z","description":"Change .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md to instruct a top-N pick view (sd ready --first 10 or --priority high), falling back to the full listing only when top candidates are unclaimable. Basis: in run 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN, one sd ready --limit 200 poured ~15 KB / 126 seed lines into the planner conversation (event 47: 15,112 output bytes, ~4k tokens) just to learn which seed is top of the queue. Expected effect: less context bloat and distraction per planning pass; composes with open seed fabro-e4fa (call economy, distinct mechanism: output volume per call, not number of calls). Basis: run 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN, workflow version af625ca581c5947f51dfa5597eb67892e0bee5d71ae041130412d1a54873ce8e, commit ecbd4d47c4c6d3272035e535731bc14f61a20662","labels":["revision"]}
 {"id":"fabro-1716","title":"Auto-approve parent-spawned develop runs for trusted worker subjects","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T17:28:57.805Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T17:28:57.805Z","description":"Extend the server auto-approve policy to trusted worker subjects on parent-spawned develop runs, closing the idle approval window. Basis: run 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN sat pending(approval_required) from 16:36:39 to 16:38:58 — 2m19s, ~13% of run wall, doing nothing — even though conductor auto-approve landed same-day in commit 7fda512 (16:18 UTC); verify whether that commit's subject set covers this spawn path and extend it if not. Expected effect: ~2 min saved per run and no zombie-pending risk; the approval-TTL backstop is already filed as fabro-54f0, so this seed covers only the auto-approve mechanism. Basis: run 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN, workflow version af625ca581c5947f51dfa5597eb67892e0bee5d71ae041130412d1a54873ce8e, commit ecbd4d47c4c6d3272035e535731bc14f61a20662","labels":["revision"]}
-{"id":"fabro-2e3c","title":"engine: auto_approve not effective through the git-source intent path (children still wait approval_required)","status":"in_progress","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T17:21:38.401Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T21:13:37.881Z","description":"Conductor pass 01M1S6MSV4 passed auto_approve:true on fabro_run_create (visible in the tool-call args); git_source::intent_from_spec maps it into RunIntentArgs.auto_approve, but BOTH children (develop 01M1S6VRWQ, revisor 01M1S9C1H8) still landed in pending/approval_required and needed manual approval (2026-09-05). The intent admission path apparently does not apply args.auto_approve as the pre-execution approval (the legacy manifest path filtered/honored it). Fix: create_run_from_intent admission must honor RunIntentArgs.auto_approve (set approval to Auto or record the approval event at admission). Blocks fully autonomous conductor children. Basis: runs 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN + 01M1S9C1H8XVVEEB62JQKPXKY3, commits 5f413bbc7/7fda51235.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
+{"id":"fabro-2e3c","title":"engine: auto_approve not effective through the git-source intent path (children still wait approval_required)","status":"closed","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T17:21:38.401Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T21:38:44.449Z","description":"Conductor pass 01M1S6MSV4 passed auto_approve:true on fabro_run_create (visible in the tool-call args); git_source::intent_from_spec maps it into RunIntentArgs.auto_approve, but BOTH children (develop 01M1S6VRWQ, revisor 01M1S9C1H8) still landed in pending/approval_required and needed manual approval (2026-09-05). The intent admission path apparently does not apply args.auto_approve as the pre-execution approval (the legacy manifest path filtered/honored it). Fix: create_run_from_intent admission must honor RunIntentArgs.auto_approve (set approval to Auto or record the approval event at admission). Blocks fully autonomous conductor children. Basis: runs 01M1S6VRWQMD56M1X8HWAXDSNN + 01M1S9C1H8XVVEEB62JQKPXKY3, commits 5f413bbc7/7fda51235.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"closedAt":"2026-09-05T21:38:44.449Z","closeReason":"Fixed and production-proven (commit aa5c598a9): the start handler's parent-worker approval gate now honors the resolved approval mode — args.auto_approve=true (-> ApprovalMode::Auto) starts orchestration children directly; every other parent-worker spawn keeps the anti-runaway guard. Proof: conductor pass 01M1SQYDJMHSVJYMZB3C643K7J created merge-upstream child 01M1SR27KEJGNQ which went straight to running with NO pending/approval_required. 920/920 fabro-server tests green incl. new companion tests (auto_approve starts runnable; without the flag the gate still parks)."}
